Current Task: Scope this startup idea: An AI tool that turns Figma files into production React
Return one ScopedIdea JSON object. Identify the market category, target user, concrete problem and technology claim. Write exactly one market query, exactly one community query and exactly one technical repository query. Each list holds exactly one entry, because each branch now calls its tool ONCE and there is no second attempt to correct a bad query.
The community and repository queries are sent verbatim to keyword search APIs (Hacker News Algolia and GitHub), which match on terms rather than meaning: write each as 2 to 4 plain keywords, never a sentence or a phrase lifted from the idea. Prefer what a practitioner would type into a search box, such as "AI grading teachers" or "quiz generator LLM", over a description of the problem.
Because it is the only attempt, each keyword query must be deliberately broad rather than specific. Choose the broadest phrasing that is still about this problem: name the capability and the user, and drop every qualifier the idea happens to mention. A narrow query does not fail loudly - it returns zero results, and zero results are scored as "nobody has this problem", which is a REJECT about your wording rather than about the idea. Measured on this system: "AI tool creates educational materials assessment" returned nothing while "AI grading teachers" returned five usable threads for the same idea. The market query is the exception and may be a phrase, because Firecrawl matches on meaning rather than on terms. List 3 to 5 assumptions and at least one unresolved scoping gap. Use today's ISO 8601 date for as_of.
